1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:02,869
Today we meet the whole numbers. We will count

2
00:00:02,869 --> 00:00:05,711
objects, discover what zero really means, and learn about

3
00:00:05,711 --> 00:00:10,502
the predecessor and successor of a number. Let's begin

4
00:00:10,502 --> 00:00:11,891
with a pencil box!

5
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:16,498
Look at this pencil box. It has three pencils.

6
00:00:16,498 --> 00:00:20,358
One pencil is taken out, so two remain. Another

7
00:00:20,358 --> 00:00:22,936
pencil goes, and just one is left. Now the

8
00:00:22,936 --> 00:00:25,330
last pencil is taken away, and the box is

9
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:28,421
empty. So what number tells us how many pencils

10
00:00:28,421 --> 00:00:31,421
are in the box now? Zero!

11
00:00:32,123 --> 00:00:35,803
How do we count things? We say one, two,

12
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:39,826
three, four, and we never stop. These counting numbers

13
00:00:39,826 --> 00:00:43,521
have a name: they are the natural numbers. We

14
00:00:43,521 --> 00:00:46,463
write them as the set one, two, three, four

15
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:49,353
and so on. But our empty box needed a

16
00:00:49,353 --> 00:00:52,503
number of its own. So zero joins the collection,

17
00:00:52,503 --> 00:00:55,283
and we get zero, one, two, three, four and

18
00:00:55,283 --> 00:00:59,263
so on. This larger family is called the whole

19
00:00:59,263 --> 00:01:03,622
numbers. Whole numbers are the natural numbers together with

20
00:01:03,622 --> 00:01:04,354
zero.

21
00:01:04,997 --> 00:01:07,443
Now let us place the two collections one above

22
00:01:07,443 --> 00:01:10,353
the other and compare them. The numbers one, two,

23
00:01:10,353 --> 00:01:13,437
three, four and five match exactly. There is only

24
00:01:13,437 --> 00:01:16,457
one new member, and that is zero. So the

25
00:01:16,457 --> 00:01:20,211
smallest natural number is one, and the smallest whole

26
00:01:20,211 --> 00:01:23,840
number is zero. And every natural number is also

27
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:27,248
a whole number: N is a subset of W.

28
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:30,700
Now let us put the whole numbers on a

29
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,224
line. This is the whole number line, and zero

30
00:01:33,224 --> 00:01:36,080
is its starting point. Then come one, two, three,

31
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:40,300
four, and we keep going: five, six, seven, eight,

32
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,880
nine, ten, and on. The arrow shows that the

33
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:47,160
whole numbers never end. Every step to the right

34
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,702
is one more, so the number on the right

35
00:01:49,702 --> 00:01:53,577
is always greater. Remember, zero is the starting point

36
00:01:53,577 --> 00:01:55,491
of the whole number line.

37
00:01:56,150 --> 00:02:00,610
Let us look closely at one number. Take nine.

38
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:02,654
One step to the right is ten, so ten

39
00:02:02,654 --> 00:02:05,700
is the successor of nine. One step to the

40
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:08,787
left is eight, so eight is the predecessor of

41
00:02:08,787 --> 00:02:11,953
nine. The successor is the next number, and the

42
00:02:11,953 --> 00:02:16,477
predecessor is the previous number. In general, the successor

43
00:02:16,477 --> 00:02:18,910
of a number n is n plus one, and

44
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,901
its predecessor is n minus one.

45
00:02:21,407 --> 00:02:25,567
Now a very important question. What comes before one?

46
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:27,622
In the whole numbers, one minus one is zero.

47
00:02:27,622 --> 00:02:31,330
But remember, zero is not a natural number, it

48
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:34,955
is a whole number. So among the natural numbers,

49
00:02:34,955 --> 00:02:38,132
one has no predecessor. In the whole numbers, the

50
00:02:38,132 --> 00:02:41,907
predecessor of one is zero. And what is the

51
00:02:41,907 --> 00:02:45,996
predecessor of zero? There is no whole number before

52
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:49,124
zero, so zero has no predecessor in the whole

53
00:02:49,124 --> 00:02:51,913
numbers. But zero does have a successor: zero plus

54
00:02:51,913 --> 00:02:52,518
one is one.

55
00:02:53,163 --> 00:02:58,037
Let us practise with bigger numbers. Take thirteen. One

56
00:02:58,037 --> 00:03:01,617
less is twelve, and one more is fourteen. Now

57
00:03:01,617 --> 00:03:04,800
take nine hundred and ninety nine. One less is

58
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,661
nine hundred and ninety eight, and one more is

59
00:03:07,661 --> 00:03:10,995
one thousand. The rule works even when the number

60
00:03:10,995 --> 00:03:12,534
of digits changes.

61
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,460
Numbers describe real things. Our box has four pencils.

62
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,580
Add one pencil and we have five, so five

63
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,160
is the successor of four. Take the last pencil

64
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:23,505
out of a box that has one, and we

65
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:27,530
are left with zero. Adding one gives the successor;

66
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:31,980
removing one gives the predecessor, when it exists in

67
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:33,071
our collection.

68
00:03:33,693 --> 00:03:36,573
Your turn! Look at the number line. What is

69
00:03:36,573 --> 00:03:40,873
the successor of eleven? And what is the predecessor

70
00:03:40,873 --> 00:03:42,564
of five? Pause the video and try both.

71
00:03:47,727 --> 00:03:50,327
Let us check. Eleven plus one is twelve, so

72
00:03:50,327 --> 00:03:54,127
the successor of eleven is twelve. Five minus one

73
00:03:54,127 --> 00:03:56,607
is four, so the predecessor of five is four.

74
00:03:56,607 --> 00:04:01,767
And one last question: does zero have a predecessor

75
00:04:01,767 --> 00:04:05,323
in the whole numbers? No, because the whole number

76
00:04:05,323 --> 00:04:07,018
line begins at zero.

77
00:04:07,483 --> 00:04:10,379
Let us recap. The counting numbers, one, two, three

78
00:04:10,379 --> 00:04:14,217
and so on, are the natural numbers. When zero

79
00:04:14,217 --> 00:04:17,093
joins them we get the whole numbers: zero, one,

80
00:04:17,093 --> 00:04:20,733
two, three and so on. The successor of a

81
00:04:20,733 --> 00:04:23,775
number is one more, and the predecessor is one

82
00:04:23,775 --> 00:04:26,643
less, where it exists. And zero is the smallest

83
00:04:26,643 --> 00:04:31,003
whole number, with no predecessor. Whole numbers are natural

84
00:04:31,003 --> 00:04:33,594
numbers plus zero. Thank you for watching!
